// slib.pssl.lib - Query CIRCL Passive SSL and model the results.
//
// Runs asroot (gated by the slib.pssl.user perm) so it can read the credentials saved by
// slib.pssl.admin.key without users being able to read them.
//
// API docs: https://www.circl.lu/services/passive-ssl/
//
// Endpoints, all GET with HTTP Basic auth (as of 2026-11, see tests/pkgs/pssl/cassettes/ for
// real responses):
//
//   /query/<ipv4 or cidr>  The certificates seen on each IP. Only IPv4, /23 to /32.
//       {"<ip>": {"certificates": [<sha1>, ...],
//                 "subjects": {"<sha1>": {"values": ["C=JP, ST=Tokyo, ..., CN=..."]}}}}
//       An IP with no certificates is missing, so an empty result is {}.
//
//   /cquery/<sha1>  The IPs a certificate was seen on.
//       {"seen": [<ip>, ...], "hits": <int>, "certificate": <sha1>}
//       An unknown SHA1 is {"seen": [], "hits": 0, ...}.
//
//   /cfetch/<sha1>  The certificate.
//       {"pem": <PEM str>,
//        "info": {"subject", "issuer", "fingerprint", "not_before", "not_after", "keylength",
//                 "key", "extension": {<openssl style extension text>}},
//        "icsi": {"first_seen", "last_seen", "times_seen", "validated", "version"}}
//
// Errors are HTTP 400s with a text/html body, ex. "Maximum CIDR block size reached >/23",
// "IPv6 is not (yet) supported", "Not existing certificate", "Incorrect format of the
// certificate fingerprint (expected SHA1 in hex format)". A 401 is bad or missing credentials.

$URL = "https://www.circl.lu/v2pssl"

